{{Quote|Soon, the warlords were dead, and I ruled in their place. It was on Rattatak that Dooku found me, and I him.|Asajj Ventress, reminiscing on her life on Rattatak|<ref name="Dark Disciple" />}}
'''Rattatak''' was a [[mountain]]ous [[planet]] located in [[the galaxy]]'s [[Outer Rim Territories]]. After [[Death|killing]] the [[warlord]]s responsible for the death of [[Jedi Knight]] [[Ky Narec]], former [[Jedi]] [[Padawan]] [[Asajj Ventress]] ruled Rattatak until she was found and recruited by former [[Jedi Master]] [[Count]] [[Dooku]], a [[Sith Lord]].

==Description==
{{Quote|I originally served in the Western Reaches. On Rattatak.|An [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[controller]], to [[Han Solo]]|<ref name="Choose Your Destiny" />}}
[[File:Rattatak_village.png|thumb|left|250px|A Rattataki Village]]
Located in the [[the galaxy]]'s [[Outer Rim Territories]], in grid square H-16 on the [[Standard Galactic Grid]],<ref name="Appendix" /> Rattatak<ref name="Trivia Gallery">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/nightsisters-trivia-gallery|text="Nightsisters" Trivia Gallery}} {{C|Slide 3}}</ref> was a [[mountain]]ous [[planet]] [[orbit]]ed by at least one [[moon]].<ref name="The Complete Season Three" /> It was the [[homeworld]] of the [[Rattatakian redjacket]].<ref name="So You Want to Be a Jedi?" />

==History==
{{Quote|I see such attentions as an investment in our Empire's future. Someday, I hope, we will achieve perfect rule and perfect peace, from here on Coruscant to the farthest systems of Lothal, Paucris, Rattatak&mdash;or whatever worlds we may yet find.|Governor Wilhuff Tarkin, to Princess [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]]|<ref name="Leia, Princess of Alderaan">''[[Leia, Princess of Alderaan]]''</ref>}}
At some point prior to the [[Clone Wars]], the [[Siniteen]] [[enslaver]] [[Hal'Sted]] was [[Death|killed]] by [[Weequay]] raiders<ref name="Nightsisters" /> during a [[Pirate uprising on Rattatak|pirate uprising]],<ref name="Nightsisters SWE">{{SWE|groups|nightsisters|Nightsisters}}</ref> leaving his [[Slavery|slave]], a young [[Dathomirian]] named [[Asajj Ventress]], orphaned. She was found by [[Ky Narec]], a [[human]]<ref name="Nightsisters" /> [[Jedi Knight]] stranded on Rattatak,<ref name="Dark Disciple" /> who recognized her potential and began to train her in the ways of [[the Force]]<ref name="Nightsisters" /> as his [[Padawan]]. For ten [[Standard year|years]], they helped the people of Rattatak, becoming enemies to some but heroes to most,<ref name="Dark Disciple" /> until he was killed while defending a Rattataki [[Rattataki Village|village]] from a Weequay raider assault, leading Ventress to give in to her grief and fall to the [[Dark side of the Force|dark side]].<ref name="Nightsisters" /> She vowed vengeance and killed the [[warlord]]s responsible for her master's death, ruling Rattatak in their place.<ref name="Dark Disciple" /> In [[23 BBY]],<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> the [[Vollick]] [[warlord]] [[Osika Kirske]] led Ventress into a trap when she attempted to kill him, using himself as bait. Ventress was captured and forced to fight in a [[Rattatak gladiatorial arena|gladiatorial arena]]. During one of Ventress' fights, the [[Dark Lord of the Sith|Sith Lord]] [[Dooku|Tyranus]] (Dooku) visited the arena in search of an [[assassin]], watching Ventress from Kirske's viewing gallery. Choosing to take Ventress as his [[Sith apprentice]], Dooku used [[Dooku's lightsaber|his lightsaber]] to behead Kirske, killing the warlord.<ref name="Dooku: Jedi Lost" />

In [[5 ABY]], near the end of the [[Galactic Civil War]], the [[New Republic]] [[starfighter]] [[squadron]] [[Shepherd Squadron]] was based on the planet.<ref name="The Ghost Ship" /> Years later, [[Teza Nasz]], a former [[Imperial officer]] and strategist, established herself as a [[warlord]] on Rattatak, uniting one of its warrior clans behind her leadership, which was a source of some complaint with [[Prime Minister]] [[Grist]] of [[Grail City]].<ref name="Resistance Reborn" />

